Open Vanilla 0030: Hero Keys, an account's own sign-in as one line of text the player keeps, and the
first step away from Discord sign-in.

The sign-in page leads with "Play now, free" (a guest) and "I have a Hero Key"; Discord and Google stay.
A new guest lands on "Your Hero Key" before the game: the key (blurred until Show), three plain lines
on what it is, Download file (OpenVanilla-HeroKey.ovkey: a short note, then the key between BEGIN/END
lines), Copy as text, and "I've saved my Hero Key" unlocking Enter the realm; "Remind me later" waits a
day. /key signs in on any device from the file or the pasted line and lands on "Welcome back" (key made,
last used, Make a new key). In the game (play.html), an account without a saved key gets one chat line
(through the page bridge: wenilla.lua -> DEFAULT_CHAT_FRAME:AddMessage) and a window over the game that
makes the key in the page; the key never passes through the game server. The play bar links the key
page (guests: "Save your heroes"). The key page also links Google to an existing account
(/auth/{provider}/start?link=1).

Keys: ovk1.<10-char id>.<32 random bytes, base64url>. Stored: hero_keys(user_id, key_id, SHA-256 of
the secret, created/saved/first used/last used, a short device name like "Chrome on Windows",
revoked_at), one working key per account (a new one revokes the old at once), and
users.hero_key_snooze_until. The secret is never stored: it is shown once, riding to a reload for 15
minutes in a cookie encrypted with the master key (wr_herokey, path /account/key, SameSite=Strict).
Checks are constant-time; key sign-in is same-site only and limited per network (20 / 15 min) and per
key id (10 / 15 min); every POST carries the session's form token.

Discord phases (prepared, not switched): DISCORD_SIGNIN=on (default: as before) | keyonly (the button
reads "Get my Hero Key with Discord", the page says Discord sign-in is retiring, and a Discord sign-in
lands on the key page until a key is saved) | off (no Discord button; Discord start and callback refuse,
pointing at the Hero Key and Google). DISCORD_RETIRE_DATE="1 December" adds the day to the notices.
Accounts keep their characters in every phase; only the way in changes.
The sign-in styles move to templates/signin_style.html, shared by login.html and the two key pages.

